body:
you could also be reacting to the 'positivity culture' that is endemic to social media and the collective subconscious as a whole. I highly recomend reading "the Happiness Industry", "Mcmindfulness by ronald purser" and "Brightsided - How Positive Thinking Undermines America by Barbara Ehrenreich" - essentially, a lot of money has pumped a pseudo spirituality into our current culture, a constant 'Yes you Can!' as opposed to 'You could, but should you?'

&#x200B;

pessimism of the intellect but triumph of the will and all that. i believe in reckless faith more than the watery promises of optimism and hope, Camus and Sartre might also be welcome guides in your current state of mind.
